Math for Trades, Volume 3 — Overgaard and Flinn (@ql-source-trades-3: 0, is #book, #part-of @ql-sources) { r_6KYSHDH6J34JT1PY43V5SYW30Q
Mark Overgaard and Chad Flinn. Math for Trades: Volume 3. BCcampus, 2022. English. Ebook ISBN 978-1-77420-173-2.

[Publisher's complete book and downloads](https://opentextbc.ca/mathfortrades3/) · [Contents](https://opentextbc.ca/mathfortrades3/table-of-contents/). CC BY 4.0 except separately identified components; credit the authors and publisher and preserve those notices.

Read all four parts, Capacities; Pressure and Total Force; Grade and Total Fall; Trigonometry, including the practice test. Chapters 10–13 develop grade and fall; 15–18 develop triangle calculations. The short pressure block is a useful unit-and-area application, not a complete fluid-mechanics treatment.

Use both the paper exercises and the publisher's answers. The PDF, EPUB, and offline quiz material let study continue without the website. Their retention is the reader's choice; the repository contains the reference only. Publisher metadata and contents checked on 28 October 2026.

